-- title:
--   Base change of a cyclotomic Drinfeld chart witness
-- statement:
--   **Numerical and cyclotomic data.** Let $q$ be a prime with $5\le q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Put $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and let $H_1=$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) be the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. For a field $F$ of characteristic $0$, [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange F (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField N₀ H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) is the intermediate field of $F$ inside the Laurent series field over $F$ generated by the coefficientwise images (under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb F`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), induced by $\mathbb Q\to F$) of the field of $q$-expansions of modular functions of level [`CohCarrier.GammaH N₀ H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ of the matrices of $\Gamma_0(N_0)$ whose diagonal unit lies in $H_1$.
--
--   **The general base.** Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ and a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi$, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field over $L$ equal to `laurentBaseChange L (xHFunctionField N₀ H₁)`. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ whose residue field is algebraically closed, such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A\to L$; $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion equal to [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) (the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-invariant, pushed into $L$), let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $t\in A$ satisfy $t^{q-1}=q\,w$ for some unit $w$ of $A$.
--
--   Write $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the scheme obtained as the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-algebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ (the algebra `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`) and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements integral over $A[j^{-1}]$ along the middle chart, with its structural morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}A$ and with `ιFin` the canonical morphism from $X_{\mathrm{fin}}=\operatorname{Spec}($`chartAlgFin A ↥K j`$)$. Let $z$ be a point of $\mathfrak X$ and let $\varpi z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathfrak X$ obtained from $\varpi$ through `toBase`; it is assumed that $\varpi z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$, so $z$ lies in the special fibre. Let $y$ be a point of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with `ιFin` mapping $y$ to $z$, and assume the supersingularity hypothesis `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` to $\Omega$ whose kernel is exactly the prime of $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The cyclotomic base.** Let $L_0$ be a field of characteristic $0$ which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of order $q\ell$, with a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta_0$ and a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi_0$; let $K_0=$ `laurentBaseChange L₀ (xHFunctionField N₀ H₁)`. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L_0$ such that $q$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta_0$ lies in the image of $A_0\to L_0$, with $K_0$ an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $A_0\to L_0$; let $j_0\in K_0$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion `coeffEmb L₀ jq`, let $\varpi_0$ generate the maximal ideal of $A_0$, let $z_0$ be a point of $\mathfrak X_0=$ `TwoChartIntegralModel A₀ ↥K₀ j₀` with $\varpi_0$'s germ $\varpi z_0$ in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z_0$, let $y_0$ be a point of the finite chart of $\mathfrak X_0$ mapping to $z_0$, and assume the same supersingularity hypothesis `hss₀` at $y_0$. No algebraic closedness is assumed of the residue field of $A_0$.
--
--   **Comparison data.** Let $i:L_0\to L$ be a ring homomorphism with $i\zeta_0=\zeta$ and $i\xi_0=\xi$; let $A$ be an $A_0$-algebra with $A_0\to A$ a local and injective homomorphism compatible with $i$ over the fraction fields, and assume $\varpi_0$ maps to $t$ times a unit of $A$. Let $cK:K_0\to K$ be a ring homomorphism acting on Laurent expansions as the coefficientwise map induced by $i$, with $cK(j_0)=j$, and let $c:$ `chartAlgFin A₀ ↥K₀ j₀` $\to$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` be a ring homomorphism compatible with $cK$ under the inclusions into $K_0$ and $K$, such that the contraction along $c$ of the prime of $y$ is the prime of $y_0$. Finally let $\beta$ be a ring isomorphism from $A\otimes_{A_0}$ `chartAlgFin A₀ ↥K₀ j₀` onto `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` with $\beta(a\otimes b)=a\cdot c(b)$; thus the finite chart algebra over $A$ is the base change of the one over $A_0$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld chart over the cyclotomic base.** Let $W_0$ be a discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\sigma_0:A_0\to W_0$ be a ring homomorphism with maximal ideal of $W_0$ generated by $\sigma_0\varpi_0$, and let $f_0,u_0,v_0\in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_0,v_0$ units and $f_0-(X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1)\in(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the form $X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₀`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)). Let
--   $$e_0:\widehat{\mathcal O}_{\mathfrak X_0,z_0}\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;W_0[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_0\varpi_0)\,v_0-f_0u_0\bigr)$$
--   be a ring isomorphism of the completion of the stalk at $z_0$ for its maximal ideal with that quotient $S_0$, and write $\mathrm{toC}_0$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mk}S_0$ for the quotient map, and $\mathrm{germ}Y_0$ for the canonical map from `chartAlgFin A₀ ↥K₀ j₀` to the stalk at $z_0$ induced by `ιFin`.
--
--   The hypothesis `hriders₀` is the conjunction of six clauses. (1) *Constants*: for every $a\in A_0$, $e_0$ carries the image in the completed stalk of the germ of the base section $a$ to the class of $C(\sigma_0 a)$. (2) *Stability of the chart*: for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K_0$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L₀ (q*ℓ) ξ₀ (q*ℓ) N₀ H₁ γ⁻¹ K₀ τ` — that is, for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ for `GammaH N₀ H₁` with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g$ having nonzero image, and all $x\in K_0$ whose Laurent expansion is that of the quotient of the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$, any embedding $\iota:L_0\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi_0=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$ satisfies: the coefficientwise $\iota$-image of the expansion of $\tau x$, times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k$ `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`, equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k$ `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`, where `conjElemN m γ` is the matrix with rows $(\gamma_{00},\gamma_{01}/m)$ and $(m\gamma_{10},\gamma_{11})$ — the subalgebra `chartAlgFin A₀ ↥K₀ j₀` is carried into itself by $\tau$. (3) *Congruence at $y_0$*: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ and $\tau$ as in (2), and given that $\tau$ preserves the chart algebra, $\tau a-a$ lies in the prime of $y_0$ for every $a$ in the chart algebra. (4) *Level automorphisms in the chart*: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau$ as in (2) preserving the chart algebra and satisfying the congruence of (3), there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S_0$, an element $c\in W_0$ (the letter is reused) and a matrix $M\in\mathrm{Mat}_2(W_0)$ such that: $\theta$ intertwines the maps $a\mapsto e_0(\mathrm{toC}_0(\mathrm{germ}Y_0\,a))$ and $a\mapsto e_0(\mathrm{toC}_0(\mathrm{germ}Y_0(\tau a)))$; $\theta$ fixes every class of a constant $C(w)$, $w\in W_0$; for each coordinate $jj$, $\theta(X_{jj})-\sum_{ii}C(M_{ii\,jj})X_{ii}$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$; $c^{q+1}-1$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; $M_{ii\,jj}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ii\,jj}$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W_0$ for all $ii,jj$; if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ then $c\equiv1$ modulo the maximal ideal; and if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity of $K_0$ then $c-1$ is a unit. (5) *Separation of branches*: for all integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and all primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S_0$ such that each $P_i$ omits at least one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, contains the class of $C(\sigma_0\varpi_0)$, and contains an element of the form $C(a_i)X_0+C(b_i)X_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and such that $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$: the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e_0$ composed with $\mathrm{toC}_0$ are distinct ideals of the stalk at $z_0$. (6) *Identification of the branch of tangent direction $(1,0)$*: for every prime $P$ of $S_0$ omitting one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, containing the class of $C(\sigma_0\varpi_0)$ and containing an element $C(1)X_0+C(0)X_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and every $a$ in the chart algebra: $\mathrm{toC}_0(\mathrm{germ}Y_0\,a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ (as a Laurent series over $L_0$) lies in the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $\hat A$ for the completion of $A$ along its maximal ideal. There exist a ring homomorphism $\psi:W_0\to\hat A$, power series $f,u,v\in\hat A[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u$ and $v$ units and $f-(X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1)\in(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e:\widehat{\mathcal O}_{\mathfrak X,z}\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;S:=\hat A[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(t)\,v-f u\bigr),$$
--   the defining element being formed from the image of $t$ in $\hat A$, such that, with $\mathrm{toC}$ the map from the stalk at $z$ to its completion, $\mathrm{mk}S$ the quotient map and $\mathrm{germ}Y$ the canonical map from `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` to the stalk at $z$, the following ten assertions hold.
--
--   (i) $\psi(\sigma_0a)$ is the image in $\hat A$ of the image of $a$ in $A$, for every $a\in A_0$. (ii) $\psi$ carries the maximal ideal of $W_0$ into the maximal ideal of $\hat A$. (iii) $f=$ `MvPowerSeries.map ψ f₀`. (iv) *Germ compatibility*: for every $x$ in `chartAlgFin A₀ ↥K₀ j₀` and every $s\in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$, if $e_0$ carries the image in the completed stalk at $z_0$ of $\mathrm{germ}Y_0\,x$ to the class of $s$, then $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}Y(c\,x)))$ is the class of `MvPowerSeries.map ψ s`. (v) *Constants*: for every $a\in A$, $e$ carries the image in the completed stalk of the germ at $z$ of the base section $a$ to the class of $C$ of the image of $a$ in $\hat A$. (vi) *Stability of the chart*: for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) N₀ H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`, the subalgebra `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` is carried into itself by $\tau$. (vii) *Congruence at $y$*: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ and $\tau$ as in (vi) preserving the chart algebra, $\tau a-a$ lies in the prime of $y$ for every $a$ in the chart algebra. (viii) *Level automorphisms in the chart*: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ as in (vi) preserving the chart algebra and satisfying the congruence of (vii), there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in\hat A$ and a matrix $M\in\mathrm{Mat}_2(\hat A)$ with: $\theta(e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}Y\,a)))=e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}Y(\tau a)))$ for all $a$ in the chart algebra; $\theta$ fixing all classes of constants $C(w)$, $w\in\hat A$; $\theta(X_{jj})-\sum_{ii}C(M_{ii\,jj})X_{ii}$ in the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, for each $jj$; $c^{q+1}-1$ in the maximal ideal of $\hat A$; $M_{ii\,jj}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ii\,jj}$ modulo the maximal ideal of $\hat A$ for all $ii,jj$; $c\equiv1$ modulo the maximal ideal whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$; and $c-1$ a unit whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity of $K$. (ix) *Separation of branches*: for all integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$ such that each omits one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, contains the class of $C$ of the image of $\varpi$ in $\hat A$, and contains an element $C(a_i)X_0+C(b_i)X_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and such that $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e$ composed with $\mathrm{toC}$ are distinct. (x) *Identification of the branch of tangent direction $(1,0)$*: for every prime $P$ of $S$ omitting one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, containing the class of $C$ of the image of $\varpi$, and containing an element $C(1)X_0+C(0)X_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and every $a$ in `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`: $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}Y\,a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of the maximal ideal of $A$ under $A\to L$.
--
--   Note that the defining equation over $\hat A$ involves the root $t$ of (a unit multiple of) $q$ of exponent $q-1$, whereas the branch conditions (ix) and (x) involve the uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A$.
--
--   This is the base-change step for the local structure of the integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M',H_1)$ at a supersingular point: a Drinfeld-type local chart $W_0[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma_0\varpi_0v_0-f_0u_0)$ of the completed stalk over a cyclotomic base $(A_0,L_0)$, together with its constant, level-equivariance and branch riders, is transported to an arbitrary discrete valuation base $A$ with algebraically closed residue field containing an element $t$ with $t^{q-1}$ a unit multiple of $q$, the defining equation becoming $C(t)v-fu$. It is used by the two statements that assemble the local chart with its level automorphisms and inertia data and with the Hasse form.
